(2052783, 277812, 28029, '<td valign="top">Sorry- I thought that I could add the recipe later,,, oops.   <br/> <br/> 8 egg yolks<br/>    1/3 cup granulated white sugar<br/>    2 cups heavy cream<br/>    1 teaspoon pure vanilla extract<br/>    1/4 cup granulated white sugar (for the caramelized tops) <br/> <br/>Preheat oven to 300ºF. In a large bowl, whisk together egg yolks and sugar until the sugar has dissolved and the mixture is thick and pale yellow. Add cream and vanilla, and continue to whisk until well blended.  <br/> <br/>Divide mixture among 6 ramekins or custard cups. Place in a water bath and bake until set around the edges, but still loose in the center, about 50 to 60 minutes. Remove from oven and leave in the water bath until cooled. Chill for a while. To serve: sprinkle   2 teaspoons of sugar over each custard. Caramelize sugar with torch . Enjoy!</td>', 'Sorry- I thought that I could add the recipe later,,, oops.     8 egg yolks    1/3 cup granulated white sugar    2 cups heavy cream    1 teaspoon pure vanilla extract    1/4 cup granulated white sugar (for the caramelized tops)  Preheat oven to 300ºF. In a large bowl, whisk together egg yolks and sugar until the sugar has dissolved and the mixture is thick and pale yellow. Add cream and vanilla, and continue to whisk until well blended.   Divide mixture among 6 ramekins or custard cups. Place in a water bath and bake until set around the edges, but still loose in the center, about 50 to 60 minutes. Remove from oven and leave in the water bath until cooled. Chill for a while. To serve: sprinkle   2 teaspoons of sugar over each custard. Caramelize sugar with torch . Enjoy!', '2006-01-18 05:40:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2052887, 278346, 34938, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, but this picture does nothing for me. I guess as they say, beauty is in the eye of the beholder. I cannot see what the fuss is all about.</td>', 'Congratulations, but this picture does nothing for me. I guess as they say, beauty is in the eye of the beholder. I cannot see what the fuss is all about.', '2006-01-18 06:40:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2052901, 276987, 35602, '<td valign="top">Thankyou all for your kind words.  I got my first goal reached for 2006, to make it to 80%.  Also my second goal, to break a six.  My last goal is to keep it consistantly in the 40-50% range overall.  Of course, that has already gone by the board, but maybe if you take all the scores from 2006, it will be there.<br/> <br/>I have to admit when I did this photo, I pretty much took it out of a recipe book and tried copying it.  I even painted a pepper shaker just like the one in the book, and I edged a napkin with yellow paint, and painted some wooden utensils ivy green.  A few things I forgot (like a little grated cheese on the side, and some over the food) but generally it came out nearly the same tones and placement as the original image.  It was absolutely delicious, but I am a veggie freak anyway.</td>', 'Thankyou all for your kind words.  I got my first goal reached for 2006, to make it to 80%.  Also my second goal, to break a six.  My last goal is to keep it consistantly in the 40-50% range overall.  Of course, that has already gone by the board, but maybe if you take all the scores from 2006, it will be there. I have to admit when I did this photo, I pretty much took it out of a recipe book and tried copying it.  I even painted a pepper shaker just like the one in the book, and I edged a napkin with yellow paint, and painted some wooden utensils ivy green.  A few things I forgot (like a little grated cheese on the side, and some over the food) but generally it came out nearly the same tones and placement as the original image.  It was absolutely delicious, but I am a veggie freak anyway.', '2006-01-18 06:46:53.000000', NULL, 0),
